#!/bin/bash

post_install() {
  cat <<'EOF'
==> virtualbox-kvm-jeffguorg-patched installed.

This build is driverless: it uses Linux KVM (/dev/kvm) and needs no
VirtualBox kernel modules. There is nothing to modprobe and no service
to enable.

Quick start with host-bridge networking:

  1. Create the host bridge once (static IP + dnsmasq on vboxbr0):
       sudo vboxbr0-setup

  2. Attach a VM to it:
       VBoxManage modifyvm <vm> --nic1 linuxbridge --nic-property1 bridge=vboxbr0
     (or select "LinuxBridge" in the GUI network settings)

  3. Run the GUI with:  VirtualBox

Notes:
  - Your user must be able to access /dev/kvm (usually via the 'kvm' group).
  - On Intel Tiger Lake and newer hosts, add 'split_lock_detect=off' to the
    kernel command line if guests appear to hang.
  - VBoxNetBrCtl is installed setuid root; it only manipulates 'vboxtap*'
    interfaces.
EOF
}

post_upgrade() {
  post_install
}
